In this folder, some data corresponding to the ground state of ethylene, water and formaldehyde are provided.
In each folder, you can find as printouts, the orbital coefficeints, the overlap (in AO), the state density in AOs and MOs.
Furthermore, the output from the CASSCF calculation in CFOUR is given, as well as its input geometry (ZMAT file). 
The data-gad.bin provides the necessary information on the states and can be read by the routine in read_cfour.py:
this gives
[n_int, n_act, n_ext]: number of internal, active and external orbitals
[n_a, n_b]: number of alfa and beta spin electrons
 ene:energy of the state
 c, C,: the c, C coefficeints associated to the CASSCF state
 S: overlap matrix
 rdm1: 1-el density matrix
 [g_ci, g_k]: Casscf gradient (CI part and orbital rotation part)
 [diag_ci, (diag_k_AI, diag_k_EI, diag_k_EA)]
 [Hx_ci, Hx_k]:Hessian-vector prodicts, Ci and orbital parts
 spin:
 mult: multiplicity

All calculations are done without point group symmetry


------------------------------------------------------
In the folder water_block2, there are the calculations done with DMRG-CASSCF in a state averaged approach.
The input file contains the geometry and the indication of the targeted spin states
the output file contains the converged energies and the associated density matriced (the orbital occupation numbers).
All calculations have been done without point-group symmetry
